WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.201
He is back on the trail.

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:03.436
74 days since announcing his third

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:04.637
bid for the White House.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:05.305
Former President

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:07.674
Trump has made his first 2024

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:09.542
campaign stop yesterday.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.311
His appearances in New Hampshire

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:12.812
and South Carolina come

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:15.315
as questions have been raised about

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:19.119
what has been so far which is a very slow

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.620
moving campaign.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.823
Concerns that he addressed head on

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:25.458
and said he's not campaigning.

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:26.893
This is like

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:29.462
about a month ago when he announced

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:32.198
well I said, you know, I got two years.

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:35.101
They said he's not doing rallies.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:36.936
He's not campaigning.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:38.772
Maybe he's lost that step.

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:39.172
We didn't

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:39.906
I'm more angry

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:41.274
now and I'm more committed

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:43.743
now than I ever was this.

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:44.310
For the record,

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.112
he announced closer to two months ago.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:48.481
But while the small scale of his events

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:49.783
yesterday were a far cry

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:51.818
from his traditionally large rallies,

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:53.386
what he chose to talk about would

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:54.687
be very familiar to you.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:56.823
We're

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:57.924
going to restore

00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:00.026
election integrity do we have to?

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:02.929
We have a woke military that can't fight

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:03.396
or win.

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:04.764
They're sending people

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:06.766
that are killers, murderers.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:07.867
They're sending rapists,

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.936
and they're sending frankly, terrorists

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:10.770
or go to New York.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.439
Nobody ever gets prosecuted.

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:13.740
I'm the only one they go after.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.742
We have men being encouraged

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:18.678
to compete against women in sports.

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:21.781
The wind turbines are all made in China.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.418
Alex Burns of

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:28.421
Politico is back with us on the panel.

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:31.724
And so are the wind turbines

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.193
killing off the bird population.

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:34.861
Which is a favorite of Trump's.

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:35.829
So, Alex,

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:37.330
this is clearly an attempt

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:38.298
to kind of

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:40.400
jumpstart his campaign,

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.435
but it was still kind of low energy.

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:43.636
Yeah, it really was.

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:45.038
And I do think, Abby, in that clip

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:46.072
that that you just played

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:47.240
is a really revealing moment

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:47.674
where he says,

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:47.874
you know,

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:48.842
they say that he's lost that,

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:51.010
but don't worry, I'm still really angry.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:52.011
You're saying

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:53.680
it's not really the point

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:54.314
here, right,

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:55.315
that I don't think anybody doubts

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:56.783
that Donald Trump is a pretty angry man?

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.151
I think what they question is

00:01:58.151 --> 00:01:59.986
whether he is fully engaged

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:01.287
with the task of running for president,

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:03.289
the answers that he obviously is not

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:04.791
And also whether he has something to say

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.459
that's really relevant to this moment.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:06.793
Right.

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:07.627
That can really connect

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:08.428
with first

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:09.896
the Republican primary electorate

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:11.431
and then much more importantly,

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:12.765
the broader American public

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:13.399
and when you hear him

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:15.135
talking about how it's so unfair,

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:15.835
how he's getting

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:17.337
investigated in New York,

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:19.105
how the wind turbines kill birds,

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:19.806
I don't think he did

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:20.440
wind turbines

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:22.275
cause cancer at this event,

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:24.110
but I'm sure we will hear that one again.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:25.278
He just sounds like a guy

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:27.247
from a different time, right?

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:27.680
A guy who

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.716
sort of trying to do the 2016 thing,

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:31.017
but at a smaller scale

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:31.885
and with less

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:33.820
sort of organic enthusiasm around it.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:34.487
And what I will say

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:35.955
just in the vein

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:36.890
of putting an asterisk

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:37.290
on everything

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.324
I just said as

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:39.225
I covered his campaign

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:40.360
launch back in 20, 15,

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.528
and I remember for a couple of months

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:42.428
after that

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:43.196
there was a,

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:43.997
you know, fascination

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:45.431
with the spectacle of it all

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.167
but the sort of persistent question of

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:49.202
is he serious, is he really running?

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:50.470
Is he really going to go for it?

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:51.571
And in the end he did.

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:51.905
Yeah,

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:53.840
I don't think we can really

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.742
make any broad judgments

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:57.510
based on what's happening right now.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.245
But it does seem to me, David,

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:02.048
that he is responding to the environment

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:03.116
which is that other

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:04.484
people are thinking about running.

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:07.020
He responded to two of them

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:07.820
yesterday as well.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:12.225
Nikki Haley called me the other day

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:12.992
to talk to me.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.394
We'll talk to her for a little while.

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:15.094
But I said, look,

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:16.129
you know, go buy your heart

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:16.996
if you want to run.

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.097
She's publicly saying,

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:20.700
I would never run against my president.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.834
He was a great president.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:22.969
Florida was actually closed

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:24.137
for a very long period.

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:24.604
I remember

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:25.505
it closed the beaches

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:26.839
and everything else.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:27.640
You know,

00:03:28.508 --> 00:03:31.077
they're trying to rewrite history.

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:33.479
By they, he means Ron DeSantis.

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:34.080
Right.

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:36.816
It is interesting because he is

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:37.917
he's clearly searching.

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.185
I think Alex, for what you're describing

00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:39.519
as sort of

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:41.254
like a message of sorts

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:43.590
that isn't just let me revisit

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:45.091
the greatest hits.

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:46.292
And there's no doubt,

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.160
Abby, to your point,

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.394
that he's trying to fill

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:49.028
the void right now

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.029
because he's the only declared

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:51.464
presidential candidate.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:51.998
And so

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:53.800
he wants to set the terms of debate

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:57.070
for Haley and DeSantis and and and start

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:58.204
making sure

00:03:58.204 --> 00:04:00.340
that it's all playing out on his terms.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.041
I'm not sure that that will be the case,

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:04.410
but that is clearly his hope.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.411
What is also different

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:07.447
and I just think we can't

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:10.250
he is a twice impeached former president

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:12.885
who is facing a ton of legal peril

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:13.519
right now

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.355
in multiple investigations

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:16.689
that by its nature,

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:18.191
no matter how much he wants to dismiss,

00:04:18.191 --> 00:04:19.292
it makes him

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:20.960
a different Donald Trump

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:21.828
in this moment,

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:23.296
entering this third campaign

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:24.631
than we've seen him before.

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:26.165
And what exactly is the pitch

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:27.900
to voters here?

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:28.735
I mean, I guess

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:30.436
the pitches that America was great

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:31.871
when he was president

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:32.972
and he's going to make it great again.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.274
I mean, that he has kind of been

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:35.675
rehashing a lot of his old hits,

00:04:35.675 --> 00:04:36.576
policy-wise at least,

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:37.310
you know, when you listen to

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:38.111
what he's saying.

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:39.145
But I mean,

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:41.314
I do think there are too many questions

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:43.716
still about whether or not, you know,

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:44.550
I was Chris

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:45.151
what you said, Alex,

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:45.985
because I think

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:47.253
that there was a lot of skepticism

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:47.820
when he first ran.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.856
And I, I have a skeptical now, too.

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:52.091
But the one thing that keeps me

00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:53.793
still parsing is, is that, you know,

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:55.261
nobody else has entered the field yet.

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:57.063
There was a lot of enthusiasm

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:57.864
ahead of the midterms

00:04:57.864 --> 00:04:58.931
when I was out talking to voters

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.099
for Ron DeSantis.

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:01.668
People thought he could legislate that.

00:05:01.668 --> 00:05:03.202
He had a lot of Trump ideas,

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:04.304
but he could

00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:05.171
sort of speak to them

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:06.839
in a more eloquent way.

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:08.341
Ron, Atlanta has not officially entered.

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:08.741
Other people

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:09.842
are still waiting in the wings.

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:11.611
And so at least for now,

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:12.211
I mean,

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:13.946
there does seem to be this hesitation

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:15.515
within the Republican Party

00:05:16.616 --> 00:05:17.417
to see where he goes.

00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:18.951
There's absolutely a hesitation

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:20.386
on the fact of those other challengers

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:21.254
and uncomfortable

00:05:21.254 --> 00:05:22.355
even with the reality

00:05:22.355 --> 00:05:23.556
of a diminished Trump,

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:23.823
that he's

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.925
still not an easy person to run against.

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:26.993
But I think another thing

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:28.127
has really stuck out for me

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:29.929
about this version of the Trump campaign,

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:31.531
because there has been real energy

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:33.266
on the grassroots Republican side

00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:34.667
over the speaker fight

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:37.470
and over of replacing Ronna McDaniel

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:38.671
as RNC chair.

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:39.439
And Donald Trump

00:05:39.439 --> 00:05:40.807
was on the wrong side

00:05:40.807 --> 00:05:42.241
of both of those things.

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:43.576
He is not only perspective

00:05:43.576 --> 00:05:44.444
from the perspective

00:05:44.444 --> 00:05:45.878
of the Republican grassroots

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:47.347
And so not only are we talking about

00:05:47.347 --> 00:05:48.147
the candidate

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:50.550
who who is rehashing kind of old fights,

00:05:50.783 --> 00:05:51.984
but in the way that the movement

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:52.819
he has inspired

00:05:52.819 --> 00:05:53.986
has transitioned,

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:55.221
particularly since the midterms

00:05:55.221 --> 00:05:55.655
that was seen

00:05:55.655 --> 00:05:57.123
as universally disappointing.

00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:58.257
He is not speaking that

00:05:58.257 --> 00:05:59.592
same language right now.

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:00.560
And so you not only have

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:01.861
a Donald Trump disconnect,

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:02.628
what we know

00:06:02.628 --> 00:06:03.596
with the kind of Republican

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:04.564
establishment figures

00:06:04.564 --> 00:06:06.899
who blame him for those midterms

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.401
candidates elections.

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:10.036
You also have a disconnect

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:11.037
between Donald Trump

00:06:11.037 --> 00:06:13.005
and the Republican grassroots right now,

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:15.274
which is currently organized

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:16.743
which are currently been motivated

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:17.443
by things

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:18.511
where he was on these complete

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:20.012
opposite side.

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:22.815
Well, I want to get back to something

00:06:22.815 --> 00:06:24.183
that we were just discussing, which is

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:25.918
why aren't there more Republicans

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:27.954
putting their name in the hat?

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:28.755
Bob Vander

00:06:28.755 --> 00:06:31.057
Plaats, an Iowa conservative activist,

00:06:31.057 --> 00:06:31.858
told Politico

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:32.792
that I think it's going to be

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:34.394
one of those deals of who's

00:06:34.394 --> 00:06:35.395
going to break first,

00:06:35.395 --> 00:06:36.429
who, who's going to be the first

00:06:36.429 --> 00:06:37.530
announced candidate

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:39.265
once that person gets in.

00:06:39.265 --> 00:06:41.000
You'll see others follow suit.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.135
So who will it be?

00:06:42.135 --> 00:06:43.069
Will it be?

00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:44.670
Are they all waiting for decent

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:45.905
just to get in?

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:46.339
You know, it

00:06:46.339 --> 00:06:47.340
reminds me of one of those

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:48.508
sort of old martial arts movies

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:49.742
where like the bad guys run at Bruce

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:51.110
Lee one at a time, and he just hit

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:51.477
the wall.

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:54.514
And there is a collective

00:06:54.514 --> 00:06:55.481
action problem here, right?

00:06:55.481 --> 00:06:56.516
The first person to get in

00:06:56.516 --> 00:06:57.183
is going to

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:59.419
find themselves in this brutal firefight

00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:00.453
with Donald Trump.

00:07:00.453 --> 00:07:01.888
None of them really has the firepower

00:07:01.888 --> 00:07:02.622
to go up against him,

00:07:02.622 --> 00:07:04.290
except maybe Ron DeSantis

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:04.891
who seems like he's

00:07:04.891 --> 00:07:06.359
going to take his time and let Florida's

00:07:06.359 --> 00:07:08.027
legislative session play out.

00:07:08.027 --> 00:07:09.362
I do think there's a real risk

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:09.929
on the part of the other

00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:11.697
candidates of overthinking this. Right.

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:13.366
And trying to find exactly the right

00:07:13.366 --> 00:07:14.567
time to get in win at the

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:15.568
at the end of the day,

00:07:15.568 --> 00:07:16.769
if you want to beat Donald Trump,

00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:18.037
you should probably get in there

00:07:18.037 --> 00:07:19.472
and beat Donald Trump.

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:21.674
There's no good solution to this

00:07:21.674 --> 00:07:23.009
because you get into early.

00:07:23.009 --> 00:07:24.210
You'll probably get a nickname.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:26.312
You'll just be out there,

00:07:26.312 --> 00:07:28.681
your neck out there for him to attack.

00:07:28.681 --> 00:07:29.882
I totally agree with that.

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:31.217
At the same time.

00:07:31.217 --> 00:07:32.251
It's not like the Trump

00:07:32.251 --> 00:07:33.453
playbook is a mystery.

00:07:33.453 --> 00:07:34.520
Right? We all know the

00:07:35.555 --> 00:07:36.956
complex thing to

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:40.193
figure out something else to do about it.

